## Handoff #7 — 2026-03-19
**From:** Tech Lead
**To:** Product Owner
**Phase:** Phase 5 Complete — Epic 5: Webhooks Authentication Enhancement

### Completed Deliverables
- [x] Section 3.21 smoke tests (7 tests) → `scripts/smoke-test.sh`
  - 3.21.1: POST /v1/webhooks authType=API_KEY — id + authType in response
  - 3.21.2: GET response does not expose plaintext apiKey credential
  - 3.21.3: GET /v1/webhooks/{id}/metrics (OWNER → 200, fields validated)
  - 3.21.4: GET /v1/webhooks/{id}/metrics (EDITOR → 200)
  - 3.21.5: GET /v1/webhooks/{id}/metrics (VIEWER → 401/403 denied)
  - 3.21.6: PUT /v1/webhooks/{id} update authConfig → 200
  - 3.21.7: POST /v1/webhooks authType=BASIC_AUTH → authType in response
- [x] Release readiness → `docs/reviews/release-readiness-webhooks-auth.md` — **Go/No-Go: ✅ GO**

### Key Decisions Made
- All 8 Epic 5 stories (014–021) verified complete against acceptance criteria
- Security properties confirmed: AES-256-GCM at rest, credentials never returned in GET responses, decrypt failures → DLQ without retry (permanent=true)
- RBAC confirmed: VIEWER denied metrics (403), OWNER-only auth config edit in UI
- Cross-tenant isolation confirmed: all 3 metrics queries include orgId parameter
- Pre-deploy checklist documented in release readiness doc

### Open Questions for Next Agent
- [ ] `WEBHOOK_CREDENTIAL_KEY` env var — generate a production-strength key (32+ bytes base64) and document in `.env.example` or `scripts/start-local.sh` before production deploy
- [ ] Webhook Health Badge lazy-loading — deferred perf improvement for orgs with >50 webhooks; consider in next performance epic
- [ ] `secret` column removal — retained for transition; schedule removal in a future v2 cleanup migration
- [ ] Signing secret generated for all auth types — cosmetic UX cleanup deferred to v2

### Risks / Watch-outs
- `WEBHOOK_CREDENTIAL_KEY` must be set before production deploy; if missing or <32 bytes the event-service will fail to start
- V050 → V051 → V052 must be applied in order; Flyway enforces this automatically, but ensure no manual skips
- `WebhookCredentialMigrationService` runs on startup and encrypts any legacy `secret` values — verify startup log confirms migration complete before directing live traffic

### Next Agent's Starting Point
Epic 5 is fully shipped. Read `docs/reviews/release-readiness-webhooks-auth.md` for the pre-deploy checklist, then work with DevOps to generate and document the `WEBHOOK_CREDENTIAL_KEY` before next production deployment. When ready to plan the next epic, start with `docs/prd-webhooks-auth.md` v2 scope items (OAuth 2.0, Custom Header, bulk metrics endpoint) as candidate backlog.

