## Handoff #4 — 2026-03-15
**From:** Tech Lead (Release Review)
**To:** Next Epic / Product Owner
**Phase:** Phase 4 Complete — Epic 4: Space-Rule Assignment

### Completed Deliverables
- [x] `AssignRulesModal` → `frontend/src/features/spaces/components/AssignRulesModal.tsx`
- [x] `AssignToSpaceModal` → `frontend/src/features/rules/components/AssignToSpaceModal.tsx`
- [x] `SpaceDetailPage` — replaced "Create Rule" with "Assign Rules"
- [x] `RuleListPage` — added "Assign to Space" single + bulk action
- [x] `BatchActionBar` — bulk assign capability
- [x] Smoke test Section 3.19 — 3/3 new tests pass
- [x] Release readiness → `docs/reviews/release-readiness-space-assignment.md`

### Key Decisions Made
- Spaces are assignment-only containers — no rule creation from space context (ADR-006)
- `PATCH /rules/{id}/move` reused for assignment — zero new backend code
- Bulk assignment uses `Promise.allSettled` over N sequential PATCHes (acceptable for N ≤ 50)
- `CreateRuleModal` NOT deleted — still used by RuleListPage

### Open Questions for Next Agent
- [ ] Bulk assignment endpoint for N > 50 rules deferred — consider in next performance epic
- [ ] Bulk assignment partial-failure handling: toast only; no transactionality

### Risks / Watch-outs
- No backend changes in this epic — zero migration risk
- VIEWER role cannot access Assign controls (RBAC enforced via `currentUser.role !== 'VIEWER'`)

### Next Agent's Starting Point
Read `docs/project-brief-space-assignment.md` for context, then review `docs/.bmad/handoff-log.md` for full epic history before starting the next epic.

