## Handoff #2 — 2026-03-14
**From:** Tech Lead (Release Review)
**To:** Business Analyst (Epic 3)
**Phase:** Phase 4 Complete — Epic 2: Space-Scoped Rule Management

### Completed Deliverables
- [x] `PATCH /rules/{id}/move` endpoint (backend) → management-service
- [x] `SpaceDetailPage` with rule list, move/copy modals
- [x] `MoveRuleModal`, `CopyRuleModal` → `frontend/src/features/spaces/components/`
- [x] `useMoveRule`, `useCopyRule` hooks
- [x] Smoke test Section 3.17 — 9/9 new tests pass
- [x] Release readiness → `docs/reviews/release-readiness-spaces-rules.md`

### Key Decisions Made
- Use `GET /spaces/{spaceId}/rules` (not `GET /rules?spaceId=...`) for space-scoped lists (ADR-003)
- Dedicated `PATCH /rules/{id}/move` for moves — preserves history + UUID (ADR-004)
- auth-service counts rules via real-time SQL COUNT from shared DB (ADR-002)

### Risks / Watch-outs
- auth-service queries `rules` table directly — if services ever split to separate DBs, this breaks

